{{ prompt }}
ORIGINAL_TASK_END

Compute a structured proof. No markdown, no additional keys, no narrative text.
SEED_ID={{ seed_id }}
{% if task_type == "numeral_system" %}Return one JSON object only with keys task_type="numeral_system", query (integer), components (list of {"arabic": integer, "roman": string}), answer (string). Decompose the query into Roman place-value pieces, then concatenate. Every component must be a canonical Roman numeral and their Arabic values must sum to query.{% endif %}
{% if task_type == "gravity" %}Return one JSON object only with keys task_type="gravity", g_estimates (list of numbers in example order), g_ols (number), query_t (original time string), query_distance (number before rounding), answer (string). Compute each g_i=2*d_i/t_i^2, then g_ols=2*sum(t_i^2*d_i)/sum(t_i^4), then query_distance=0.5*g_ols*query_t^2. Give intermediate values to at least six significant digits.{% endif %}
{% if task_type == "equation_numeric" %}Return one JSON object only with keys task_type="equation_numeric", rules (operator to public rule name), example_outputs (list of strings in example order), query_output (string), answer (string). Choose one valid global assignment, recompute every example and the query; keep operator prefixes/suffixes. All non-join rules must share normal/flip family and at most one per semantic group. Public candidates: {"operand_pattern": "AB<operator>CD with two decimal digits on each side", "parses": {"AB_CD": "left=AB, right=CD", "BA_DC": "left=reverse(AB), right=reverse(CD)"}, "operations": ["concatenate", "add", "add±1", "subtract", "reverse subtract", "absolute difference", "multiply", "multiply±1", "max mod min"], "output_formats": ["raw", "reverse digits", "operator-prefixed reverse", "two-digit padding", "operator suffix"], "rules": [{"name": "sub", "formula": "AB - CD, raw"}, {"name": "absdiff", "formula": "|AB - CD|, raw"}, {"name": "absdiff_prefix", "formula": "|AB - CD| with operator prefix"}, {"name": "join", "formula": "AB concatenated with CD"}, {"name": "join_swap", "formula": "CD concatenated with AB"}, {"name": "add", "formula": "AB + CD"}, {"name": "add_p1", "formula": "AB + CD + 1"}, {"name": "add_m1", "formula": "AB + CD - 1"}, {"name": "mul", "formula": "AB * CD"}, {"name": "mul_p1", "formula": "AB * CD + 1"}, {"name": "mul_m1", "formula": "AB * CD - 1"}, {"name": "maxmodmin", "formula": "max(AB, CD) mod min(AB, CD)"}, {"name": "flip_add", "formula": "reverse(BA + DC)"}, {"name": "flip_add_p1", "formula": "reverse(BA + DC + 1)"}, {"name": "flip_add_m1", "formula": "reverse(BA + DC - 1)"}, {"name": "flip_mul", "formula": "reverse(BA * DC)"}, {"name": "flip_mul_p1", "formula": "reverse(BA * DC + 1)"}, {"name": "flip_mul_m1", "formula": "reverse(BA * DC - 1)"}, {"name": "flip_absdiff", "formula": "reverse(|BA - DC|)"}, {"name": "flip_maxmodmin", "formula": "reverse(max(BA, DC) mod min(BA, DC))"}, {"name": "flip_sub_prefix", "formula": "reverse(BA - DC), preserving a negative sign as an operator prefix"}, {"name": "flip_sub_suffix", "formula": "reverse(DC - BA), appending the operator for a negative result"}, {"name": "flip_absdiff_prefix", "formula": "operator-prefixed reverse(|BA - DC|)"}, {"name": "flip_absdiff_suffix", "formula": "reverse(|BA - DC|) followed by the operator"}], "global_constraints": ["All non-join rules in one prompt use either normal or flipped operand family.", "At most one non-join rule from each semantic group: sub_or_mod_like, add_like, mul_like.", "Join and reverse-join are the join_like exception and can coexist with the other groups.", "A query operator absent from examples is Guess; it is admitted only when all valid assignments give one query output."]}{% endif %}
